hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"196","On emancipation: Muhammad ibn Rafi and Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Umar ibn Hawshab informed us, Isma'il narrated to me - and Yahya said: Isma'il ibn Umayyah - then both agreed: from his father, from his grandfather, who said: They had a slave called Tahman - or Dhakwan - and his grandfather freed half of him, so the slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You become free in your freedom and remain a slave in your slavery. So he would serve his master until he died; Yahya added: meaning he was a slave one month and free one month. Abu Dawud said: His grandfather is Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-As."
